{
  "abstract": "We study the genus-five cover p²=w²+1, q²=w²+lambda*w+1, h²=w²+(lambda+1/lambda)w+1 over Q(s), with lambda=2s/(1−s²), arising from order-four Diophantine bases. Its h-sign quotient is an elliptic curve of rank two. An injective specialization and an elliptic-surface height argument determine the complete Mordell–Weil lattice, including saturation, and identify its full lifting coset as aP0+bP1 with a+b odd and height a²+5b². The two least-height nondegenerate lifts have height nine and genus three. We determine every rational point on both curves. The first computation uses a rank-zero elliptic quotient. For the second, a complete squareclass descent reduces all rational points to two bielliptic genus-two curves with rank-two Jacobians. Explicit quadratic Chabauty at 3 leaves finitely many simple Hensel classes; partial saturation and complete finite-field images at 5 and 7 exclude all extra classes. The supplement records the analytic coefficient bound, minimal-model height values, exact residue data and reproducible checks. Every rational point on these two bisections is a degenerate base parameter. The result classifies this quotient lattice and its first two nonsplit lifts; it does not exclude higher-height bisections, other multisections, or rational Diophantine septuples in general.",
